		<preamble GUID="_1796a097-1de1-403c-87d8-a0c9ed4112ae" eId="preamble"><?DMS-Component componentId="18817976-2e26-4949-972e-ff367e4c7fa0" seriesId="410869dc-0adf-426c-a02e-fb11e2af33ae" versionNumber="1"?>
			
			<formula GUID="_2a0b7418-764b-447f-b1ca-5f18ec829003" eId="preamble__enactingWords" name="enactingText">
				<p>The Secretary of State makes the following <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType" /> in exercise of the powers conferred by sections 1(1) and 18(2) of the Safety of Sports Grounds Act 1975<authorialNote GUID="_1be9f82a-af01-4796-beb9-e38f583befb4" class="footnote" eId="fnote_1" marker="1">
						<p>1975 c. 52; section 1(1) was amended by Schedule 2 to the Fire Safety and Safety of Places of Sport Act 1987 (c. 27).</p>
					</authorialNote>.</p>
				<p>The Secretary of State is of the opinion that the condition in section 1(1) of that Act is satisfied<authorialNote GUID="_caa0ba5a-4141-4682-bacb-aacea33a8779" class="footnote" eId="fnote_2" marker="2">
						<p>By section 1(1) of the Safety of Sports Grounds Act 1975, the Secretary of State may by order designate as a sports ground requiring a safety certificate under that Act any sports ground which, in the Secretary of State’s opinion, has accommodation for more than 10,000 spectators. The Safety of Sports Grounds (Accommodation of Spectators) Order 1996 (S.I. 1996/499) substituted the number 5,000 for the number of spectators specified in section 1(1) of that Act in respect of sports grounds in England and Wales at which association football matches are played and which are occupied by a football club which is a member of the Football League Limited or the Football Association Premier League Limited.</p>
					</authorialNote> and has, in accordance with section 18(4) of that Act, consulted with such persons and bodies of persons as appear requisite to the Secretary of State.</p>
			</formula>
		</preamble>
		<body><?DMS-Component componentId="6e0f06af-3378-4510-b91c-22f0f055db5e" seriesId="36c3570b-4036-4554-ae36-57f190e14f12" versionNumber="1"?>
			
			<article GUID="_1e16dd31-9334-4fc8-b1ea-9b477f12224a" class="prov1" eId="art_1"><?DMS-Component componentId="7cff3bbf-f4a8-47b6-a5ed-5ea40f6c0982" seriesId="40288e96-b5cf-4e2a-b041-8118a35a68ad" versionNumber="1"?>
				
				<heading GUID="_c19ca580-a734-4e9c-b9ea-eb08721f93c9" eId="art_1__hdg">Citation, commencement and extent</heading>
				<num>1.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_d03d17f6-07ab-460b-b4fc-5cf628d42b8d" class="prov2" eId="art_1__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>This Order may be cited as the Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) (Amendment) (England) (No. 2) Order 2023 and comes into force on 8th May 2023.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_228bd173-aabc-49c9-a21d-994f89aafe89" class="prov2" eId="art_1__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>This Order extends to England and Wales.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</article>
			<article GUID="_5038ce11-2e7c-4ab8-9a45-0ef6647420a6" class="prov1" eId="art_2"><?DMS-Component componentId="11185c71-487a-4db2-a87d-600cf0cb0deb" seriesId="1164cac1-c96e-4722-8811-de0273f667d2" versionNumber="1"?>
				
				<heading GUID="_471d0f8f-b83d-4e37-8749-290caad33b3b" eId="art_2__hdg">Amendments to the Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) Order 2015</heading>
				<num>2.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_ed4eae0f-a990-412c-9d8d-d7aac402e363" class="prov2" eId="art_2__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>The Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) Order 2015<authorialNote GUID="_d93651fa-8471-483d-9110-fb53a15730c7" class="footnote" eId="fnote_3" marker="3">
								<p>S.I. 2015/661, amended by S.I. 2020/434; there are other amending instruments but none is relevant.</p>
							</authorialNote> is amended as follows.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_5ec5af61-aba7-4975-8b91-e914be40f5d3" class="prov2" eId="art_2__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<intro GUID="_d6caa5fa-28b4-4d32-9863-76d82ce32e45" eId="art_2__para_2__intro">
						<p>In Schedule 2 (sports grounds designated under article 2(2))—</p>
					</intro>
					<level GUID="_c2034ca2-cb84-4bb3-9311-3ea388f9e58e" class="para1" eId="art_2__para_2__para_a">
						<num>(a)</num>
						<content>
							<p>in the first column of the entry for Brentford Community Stadium<authorialNote GUID="_26f3a1d2-3fbd-4e94-b6f6-6ba0165f886f" class="footnote" eId="fnote_4" marker="4">
									<p>The entry for Brentford Community Stadium was inserted by S.I. 2020/434.</p>
								</authorialNote>, occupied by Brentford Football Club and London Irish Rugby Football Club, for “Brentford Community Stadium” substitute “Gtech Community Stadium”;</p>
						</content>
					</level>
					<level GUID="_c1f35064-5e77-4749-8793-4751135a6c5f" class="para1" eId="art_2__para_2__para_b">
						<num>(b)</num>
						<content>
							<p>for the first column of the entry for White Hart Lane, occupied by Tottenham Hotspur Football Club, substitute “Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, 782 High Road, London, N17 0BX”.</p>
						</content>
					</level>
				</paragraph>
			</article>
			<hcontainer GUID="_61deb88c-e19e-405a-ae2e-db339bc4efe4" eId="sigs" name="signatures"><?DMS-Component componentId="9952acac-dfbb-46b0-a00e-ab45f8349e56" seriesId="00f8ff9b-fe9c-412d-9303-801c5958e47d" versionNumber="0"?>
				
				<hcontainer GUID="_8a89081b-a49a-4cc4-9e7d-9ce8e3b95202" eId="sigs__sigBlk" name="signatureBlock">
					<content>
						<block GUID="_6e7be397-d399-4383-a75e-49076f91c47d" eId="sigs__sigBlk__sig" name="signature">Lucy Frazer</block>
						<block GUID="_93300a81-8b34-4f63-aebf-80b6a4a87812" eId="sigs__sigBlk__role" name="role">Secretary of State</block>
						<block name="date"><date date="2023-04-12">12th April 2023</date></block>
						<block GUID="_b5cbe81f-deee-4e11-a99d-0f9b68506939" eId="sigs__sigBlk__org" name="organization">Department for Culture, Media and Sport</block>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
			</hcontainer>
